---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Overview"
  description="OpenDock is an open-source, privacy-first smart dock for Windows with live widgets, local automations, and no mandatory account."
>
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="container hero-grid">
      <div class="hero-copy">
        <div class="hero-badges">
          <span class="badge">MIT licensed</span>
          <span class="badge">Runs locally</span>
          <span class="badge">No account</span>
        </div>
        <h1>Not another taskbar clone. A dock you own.</h1>
        <p class="lead">
          OpenDock brings live widgets, layout persistence, and programmable automations to
          Windows—without a subscription, license server, or hidden telemetry.
        </p>
        <div class="hero-cta">
          <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/docs/#download">Download for Windows</a>
          <a class="btn btn-secondary" href="https://github.com/isaacobenzy/OpenDock">View on GitHub</a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="dock-preview" aria-hidden="true">
        <div class="dock-bar">
          <div class="dock-pill accent">16:42</div>
          <div class="dock-pill">CPU 12%</div>
          <div class="dock-pill">Tasks 3</div>
          <div class="dock-pill">Weather</div>
          <div class="dock-pill">+</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <h2>Widgets that cooperate, not compete</h2>
      <p class="section-intro">
        Calendar, tasks, system health, and optional integrations share context so OpenDock can
        act before you open five different apps.
      </p>
      <div class="card-grid">
        <article class="card">
          <h3>Local automations</h3>
          <p>Event-condition-action rules run on your PC with quiet hours, cooldowns, and explicit permissions.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <h3>Permissioned widget SDK</h3>
          <p>Built-in widgets ship first; extensions declare capabilities up front instead of getting full native access.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <h3>Exportable setup</h3>
          <p>Back up layouts and settings, move between machines, and recover gracefully from invalid configuration.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container comparison">
      <h2>Why teams pick OpenDock</h2>
      <p class="section-intro">Inspired by the smart dock category, engineered for transparency and control.</p>
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th scope="col">Capability</th>
            <th scope="col">OpenDock</th>
            <th scope="col">Typical proprietary dock</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <th scope="row">License</th>
            <td>MIT, free forever</td>
            <td>Paid lifetime or subscription</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <th scope="row">Account</th>
            <td>Not required</td>
            <td>Often required for activation</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <th scope="row">Telemetry</th>
            <td>None by default</td>
            <td>Often unclear or bundled</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <th scope="row">Automation rules</th>
            <td>User-defined ECA engine</td>
            <td>Fixed preset toggles</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <th scope="row">Extension model</th>
            <td>Manifest + permissions</td>
            <td>Closed ecosystem</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container cta-band">
      <h2>Ready to try the Milestone 2 prototype?</h2>
      <p class="section-intro">
        The desktop app includes a floating dock, live clock, persisted layout, and Windows fullscreen
        behavior. Widget gallery and SQLite land in the next milestones.
      </p>
      <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/docs/">Read the docs</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
